You submit time
- JavaScript catches the form
- fetch("/api/results") sends it to Laravel
- ResultController receives it
- Result model saves it
- MySQL stores it permanently
- JS reloads results from database
- leaderboard updates

Leaderboard
-formats time cleanly
-sorts fastest first
-calculates rank inside its own category
-shows all results when filters are All
-keeps ranks correct per game/track/category
-lets you delete results
-saves permanently in database

Laravel     -*- Backend
MySQL       -*- Memory/Stores Results
HTML/CSS/JS -*- Frontend
Git+GitHub  -*- tracks code locally+stores it online
Railway     -*- Loads code stored in Github,
                runs trough Laravel and gives URL
Dockerfile  -*- Instructs how to run the app

My PC → code editor only
GitHub → source of truth
Railway → live app server
MySQL (Railway) → live database
